          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: اون",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اون — ūn — \"wool\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سردیوں میں ہم اون کے سویٹر پہنتے ہیں۔ sardiyoṅ meṅ ham ūn ke sveṭar pahante haiṅ. In winter we wear woollen jumpers."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اون (ūn) is inherited from Sanskrit ūrṇā, \"wool\" (CDIAL 2424)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
